# `prettier --check .` formats the whole tree; this file is what it leaves out.
# Prettier also reads .gitignore, so untracked local files (node_modules, dist,
# docs/superpowers/, scripts/local/, ...) are already skipped.

# Auto-generated files
src/**/*.generated.ts

# Written by tools, not by hand. A Prettier pass would fight the writer:
# sync-manifest emits JSON.stringify(_, null, 2), which Prettier reflows (short
# arrays onto one line), so the next `bun run sync-manifest` would fail
# format:check. package-lock.json is npm's.
manifest.json
package-lock.json

# Prose. Formatting all Markdown is about 4,600 changed lines across 150 files,
# mostly table realignment and list/emphasis markers, which would bury the code
# changes in review and churn every open docs/skills branch. skills/*.md is also
# parsed by check:skills (tables, frontmatter), and docs/ holds the bug corpus
# that check:bug-corpus parses plus docs/index.html, whose markup
# check:tool-counts reads. Left out deliberately (#813); format them in a
# dedicated PR if that trade changes.
*.md
docs/

# Sibling git worktrees live under .claude/worktrees/ in the primary checkout.
# Without this, `prettier --check .` run there would walk every other branch.
.claude/worktrees/
